External artifacts

The recipe tool downloads and builds llama.cpp from a pinned public revision. llama.cpp is MIT licensed. Its LICENSE is retained in the generated runtime archive. Source: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp.

Model weights and runtime images are referenced by immutable revisions/digests. They are downloaded only during deployment, not embedded or redistributed in this repository. Each GGUF recipe folder has a NOTICE for its model terms.

Qwen3.8-27B-FP8: Apache-2.0, https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B-FP8 .
NVIDIA Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4: Apache-2.0, https://huggingface.co/nvidia/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4 .
Qwen3.8-Flash-Next: Qwen Community License 1.0, https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next/blob/main/LICENSE . The RadixArk NVFP4 derivative declares license "other" and refers to upstream terms: https://huggingface.co/RadixArk/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4 . This custom model license is outside the repository standard allowlist. Review upstream terms before downloading or redistributing weights; these recipes do not establish downstream license compatibility.

SGLang: Apache-2.0, https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang . The container image includes additional upstream components under their respective terms. This recipe does not redistribute image contents. Container digests and model revisions are in catalog.json. The Flash-Next runtime is the cookbook's development build, not a claim of stable-release qualification.

Local test dependencies: PyYAML (MIT, https://pyyaml.org/) and jsonschema (MIT, https://github.com/python-jsonschema/jsonschema). They are used for YAML and CRD schema validation only.

NVIDIA container images retain their upstream terms. Access to a public image reference does not grant credentials or image redistribution rights. No third-party runtime binaries, images or model weights are embedded in this tool.
